section('parameters','Tool and exact-parameter assessment')
p('Commands below are transcribed from actual logs where available. Saved recipes are explicitly labelled: an error in a recipe does not by itself prove that an existing output was produced by that command. Versions are reported where observed, not inferred from present installations.')
for k,title in [('genome','Genome concatenation'),('markers','Three-marker concatenation'),('rpb2','RPB2 alone'),('snp','Legacy SNP alignment')]:
    add('<h3>'+title+'</h3><pre>'+esc('\n'.join(E['trees'][k]['log_evidence']))+'</pre>')
p('The three full-sequence analyses use valid automatic model selection. They contain constant sites, so an SNP-only ascertainment correction should not be added. Their current commands provide neither support resampling nor gene partitions. The SNP-only GTR+ASC setting is appropriate for a truly variable-site alignment, but cannot repair missing-as-reference preprocessing. Composition failures are diagnostics requiring sensitivity checks, not an automatic reason to delete samples. '+web('https://iqtree.github.io/doc/Command-Reference','IQ-TREE command reference')+'.')
p('For a validated marker alignment, use a verified three-locus partition definition with model selection, support calculations and a fixed seed. For 4,661 core loci, benchmark partition/model merging or an explicitly justified simpler model; blindly requesting exhaustive per-locus model searches can be unnecessarily expensive. A candidate command, not executed in this review, is:')
add('<pre>iqtree -s validated_concat.fa -p verified_partitions.nex -m MFP+MERGE -B 1000 -alrt 1000 -seed 20261110 -nt AUTO --prefix NEW_RELEASE/core</pre>')
p('Support values should be displayed only after computation and convergence review. Consider a protein-based backbone and gene-tree concordance for species-level placement, and a more closely related within-terreus panel for fine population structure. Preserve a full section-level overview with eligible references.')
