section('code','Code findings: confirmed defects versus unresolved provenance')
table(['Finding','Evidence / impact','Sensible correction'],[
 ['Missing genotypes changed to reference — confirmed in data','Both inspected merged and filtered VCF headers contain <code>bcftools … setGT … -t . -n 0</code>. One inspected first record has 43 reference genotypes with missing AF/DP/AD.','Generate reference calls from callable evidence, preserve unknowns, apply repeat/quality masks and use a denominator of shared callable sequence. '+web('https://www.htslib.org/doc/bcftools.html','bcftools documentation')],
 ['Raw-read availability false negatives — confirmed','build_complete_inventory.py searches fastp */*_1.fastq.gz and misses local R1/R2 names. Raw paired files exist for 11, 26 and R22 despite FASTA-only labels.','Discover all supported naming conventions from an explicit manifest; distinguish raw reads present, preprocessing complete and analysis eligible.'],
 ['QC reuse and completion checks — code risk','Reuse is based on labels/summary presence rather than input hash; expected 66/59 and older 28 counts are hardcoded; summary scripts do not reject missing rows.','Validate identity, exit state and expected manifest rows before a completion marker. Do not silently use the first matching summary.'],
 ['Dendrogram-to-Newick conversion — code defect','The notebook assigns dist/2 to every child, including internal nodes. Internal branch lengths require parent height minus child height.','Correct conversion and verify pairwise cophenetic heights; do not assume current Newicks have valid distances without checking their exact generating code.'],
 ['Inconsistent functional analyses — confirmed notebook state','Older Aug25 OG mapping and obsolete 0_8_dbscan path; saved KeyError; Ward on scaled data versus 30-cluster agglomeration on unscaled data; generic Diagnosis colourbar without corresponding encoded categories.','One frozen input table, explicit transform and distance, justified cluster display, sample-order assertions, explained variance and truthful legends. Ward requires Euclidean geometry; use average/complete linkage for Jaccard. '+web('https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.cluster.hierarchy.linkage.html','SciPy linkage documentation')],
 ['Functional ratios labelled as enrichment — inferential problem','Cluster mean divided by other mean plus 1e-10 can create extreme ratios; it is not a hypothesis test.','Show effect sizes/prevalence first; if testing, define a background, model phylogenetic/population dependence, correct multiple testing and report sample sizes.'],
 ['Gene IDs truncated to 14 characters — current check passes','All 711,868 EffectorP rows tested match the first whitespace-delimited identifier. No current collision was demonstrated by this check.','Use full tokens and isolate-namespaced gene IDs for robustness; do not describe this as a proven present-data failure.'],
 ['Older InterPro and lov-cluster code — limited scope','Jun23 OG IDs and hardcoded absence thresholds refer to older cohorts. Multi-column explode assumes equal copy-list lengths. Keyword grep is not orthology; append redirection can duplicate results and substring matches can confuse IDs.','Use gene-level namespaced mappings, stable OG release IDs and explicit locus coordinates. Validate lov-cluster synteny, homology and contig boundaries; rescue apparent absences in genomic sequence.'],
 ['Workflow configuration / recipes — not a reproducible executable pipeline','config.yaml has missing mapping colons; saved BRAKER species name is unquoted; all-site shell recipe contains invalid assignment syntax; several paths refer to renamed or historical directories.','Repair syntax and paths in a future working release. Actual logs take precedence; do not infer that all stored results are invalid merely from broken recipes.'],
 ['Mitochondrial reference mismatch — configuration ambiguity','A configured JAAWWR identifier conflicts with the NIH2624 CH981540.1 scaffold used in a step; inspected CH981540.1 FASTA identifies mitochondrial scaffold.','Pin the intended reference assembly and mitochondrial contig by accession/header/hash. Document nuclear/mitochondrial masking consistently.'],
 ['MST plotting — presentation defect, graph algorithm passes','Notebook uses stale snp-dists_output.tsv path instead of distances.tab and draws nodes twice, obscuring labels. Independent Kruskal check confirms the stored graph minimum total.','Retain the graph check, resolve source distances, draw once with readable labels, meaningful edge lengths/weights and a cohort legend.']])
p('The all-site variant area contains only one inspected sample directory, not a complete cohort callability release. A command that retains nonvariant positions still needs coverage-based handling of missing sites. The artifact counts above should not be interpreted as validation of every BAM, VCF or predicted event.')
end()

section('figures','Figure assessment and recommended publication portfolio')
p('The four existing QC PNGs were visually reviewed alongside the current MST, BiG-SCAPE heatmap, stored notebook graphics and the Klebsiella/Listeria comparators. The main deficiencies are cohort coverage and provenance; a cosmetic redraw alone will not resolve them.')
table(['Existing visual','Assessment','Recommended change'],[
 [local('terreus_qc_check/figures/figure1_busco_completeness.png','BUSCO completeness'),'Useful stacked C/S/D/F/M presentation for 28 assemblies, with internal-stop diagnostics. Some narrow facet labels are clipped.','Expand to the frozen cohort; preserve lineage/mode; investigate internal-stop predictions without equating them directly with biological pseudogenes.'],
 [local('terreus_qc_check/figures/figure2_assembly_metrics.png','Assembly metrics'),'Clear size, scaffold count, N50 and GC panels; low-contiguity assemblies are apparent. Only the older cohort is represented.','Retain log scales where labelled; add all eligible reference genomes and use consistent sample order across panels.'],
 [local('terreus_qc_check/figures/figure3_read_support.png','Read support'),'Readable basic metrics; very high depth>0 breadth can coexist with poor genome completeness. Narrow percentage axes emphasize small differences.','State exact quality filters and depth denominator; add useful depth-threshold breadth. Keep genome-only references visible elsewhere with read metrics not applicable.'],
 [local('terreus_qc_check/figures/figure4_integrated_qc.png','Integrated QC'),'Helpful overview of the older 28-sample subset, not the expanded release.','Update from a canonical manifest; any 95% BUSCO guide should be explained as a chosen screening criterion, not a universal pass/fail law.'],
 [local('results/0_6_1_bigscape/bigscape.png','BiG-SCAPE heatmap'),'Dense family matrix with limited readable labelling/legend and problematic transparent-background display.','Use a white background, explicit present/absent/unknown legend, selected labels and metadata tracks; separate family clustering from organism phylogeny.'],
 [local('results/0_5_mst/mst.png','MST'),'Large overlapping nodes and labels obscure a mathematically valid stored MST.','Resolve distance provenance first, then redraw once with readable labels, cohort annotations and edge units.'],
 ['Stored functional PCA/dendrograms','Older inputs, generic colourbar and inconsistent clustering definitions limit both interpretation and reproducibility.','Rebuild after code/input repairs; show explained variance and distinguish exploratory clustering from evolutionary relationships.']])
p('<strong>Recommended main presentation:</strong> a supported circular phylogeny with a restrained set of metadata rings, paired with a rectangular gene-content heatmap and a local-isolate phenotype panel. Keep the full reference context in the overview; a second within-terreus zoom improves resolution without deleting divergent references.')
table(['Priority / figure','What to display','What it answers / prerequisite'],[
 ['1 · Cohort and QC overview','Rows: all eligible assemblies plus documented exclusions. Columns: reads, assembly, primary annotation, BUSCO, markers, orthogroups, BGC, variants; adjacent size/N50/completeness bars.','Makes completeness auditable. Separate no reads, not applicable, not run, failed, ambiguous and confirmed absence. G0/G1.'],
 ['2 · Circular phylogeny','Genome tree, support symbols, species-labelled sectors only where topology permits; study/reference, MG, QC, marker availability and read availability rings.','Taxonomic context and relationship to references. No forced monophyly or invented support. Full topology now exploratory; publication after G3.'],
 ['3 · Marker recovery and concordance','66 × 3 availability/copy-status matrix, then BenA/CaM/RPB2 single-locus trees or tanglegrams against genome tree; curated type/reference labels.','Separates missing information from locus disagreement and paralogy. Availability audit supplied now; orthology gate before taxonomic interpretation.'],
 ['4 · Orthogroup architecture','Occupancy histogram; strict single-copy versus multicopy core; accessory burden; species/MG sharing using an UpSet plot with explicit prevalence definitions.','Describes the present pan-genome without treating annotation-driven absence as evolution. Current descriptive audit supplied; standardization before biological comparison.'],
 ['5 · Accessory gene-content heatmap','Jaccard distance matrix in phylogenetic tip order, with species/MG/QC/annotation tracks and accessory burden. Companion view may use average-linkage clustering of the same distances.','Distinguishes agreement with phylogeny from clustering discovered in gene content. Do not use Ward directly on a Jaccard distance matrix. Handle low-quality detection uncertainty before computing distances.'],
 ['6 · Stratified core–accessory comparison','Core patristic distance versus accessory Jaccard; panels pooled, within species, within supported lineage, between lineages; show counts, ranges and overlapping points.','Tests whether pooled correlation is driven by deep taxonomic splits. Use isolate-label matrix permutations, not independent pair shuffling or pair count as sample size. Descriptive MG analysis is safest at n=3/3/5.'],
 ['7 · Functional modules and locus context','BGC-family/CAZyme heatmap with presence, count and unknown states; a separate lov locus arrow/synteny panel with contig ends and copy numbers.','Links functions to clades while exposing fragmentation and annotation effects. Correct SignalP before secretome tracks; state BGC family cutoff and family/domain counting rules.'],
 ['8 · Local-isolate metadata / phenotypes','12-isolate aligned panel: MG, DTO, date, location and CAS/AmB/VRC/POS raw measurements. A twofold/log2 scale may be suitable after assay units are confirmed.','Connects available phenotype observations to relationships; preserves -1/-2 columns until their meaning is established. No resistant/susceptible categories inferred from workbook title.'],
 ['Supplementary · sensitivity / quality','Protein versus DNA orthology, quality-filtered versus inclusive cohort, clade-balanced rarefaction, assembly replicates, read-backed CNV and selected SNP/callability results.','Shows stability and where uncertainty originates. Additional contamination screening and read-supported QV can strengthen assembly confidence.']])
add('<figure><img src="marker_availability_audit.png" alt="Availability of three phylogenetic markers across all 66 genome-tree samples"><figcaption>New audit diagnostic from existing alignments; no phylogenetic rerun. SVG and PDF versions accompany the PNG.</figcaption></figure>')
add('<figure><img src="orthogroup_inventory_audit.png" alt="Orthogroup occupancy and mutually exclusive sharing categories"><figcaption>New descriptive audit of the existing Results_Sep28 classic orthogroup matrix. An OG detected in one sample is not necessarily a lineage-specific biological innovation.</figcaption></figure>')
add('<h3>What to borrow from the Klebsiella work</h3>')
p('I reviewed the final full-590 publication tree and its reproduction/mirror specifications under C:\\Users\\q287js\\Desktop\\Klebsiella_References. Its useful elements are the study/reference distinction, metadata rings, numbered study labels, restrained sector tinting and a complete legend. Transfer that visual grammar to fungal metadata; bacterial ST, KL and carbapenemase tracks are not relevant defaults here.')
p('<a href="'+Path(r'C:\Users\q287js\Desktop\Klebsiella_References\FINAL_PUBLICATION_CORE_FILES_20260713\01_ML_TREE_FINAL\klebsiella_final66_full590_publication_gene_legend_v3.png').as_uri()+'">Open the reviewed Klebsiella circular-tree reference</a>.')
p('The Klebsiella package documents branch compression with explicit breaks and a UFBoot correlation of 0.594. It is therefore a design reference, not automatic proof of analytical convergence. With about 66 tips, prefer a legible linear branch-length scale; if breaks are unavoidable, mark them and provide an uncompressed companion. Include support only where newly calculated and validated.')
add('<h3>What to borrow from the Listeria study</h3>')
p('The relevant comparison is the larger reproducible study in E:\\2_listeria_monocytogenes\\repro, especially final scripts 44, 46 and 47 and their protein-run figures. Its smaller historical eight-isolate run and early SYNTHESIS narrative are not the final reference. The final Jaccard figure combines phylogenetic order, metadata strips and accessory burden; this structure translates well to terreus.')
p('Reviewed Listeria references: '+ ' · '.join('<a href="'+(Path(r'E:\2_listeria_monocytogenes\repro\results\figures\n64_protein')/f).as_uri()+'">'+label+'</a>' for f,label in [('fig_jaccard_figfinal.png','Final Jaccard heatmap'),('fig_mantel_final.png','Final lineage-stratified comparison'),('fig_orthogroup_lineage_specificity.png','Orthogroup lineage specificity')])+'.')
p('Listeria uses N0 hierarchical orthogroups in its reproducible pipeline, whereas the current terreus count table contains classic OGs. Match definitions before comparing counts or “core” sizes. Listeria’s lineage-specificity plot uses prevalence 2 through floor(0.85n), Fisher tests with BH correction and an absolute prevalence difference threshold of 0.4; those are study-specific choices, not validated fungal defaults.')
p('The final Listeria stratification script uses 2,999 permutations with a fixed seed, jointly permuting square-matrix isolate labels within strata and independently permuting the two isolate axes for between-lineage rectangular comparisons. Earlier pair-vector shuffling fails to preserve pairwise dependence. The final figure also removed stronger mechanistic language. Follow the final implementation and its restrained interpretation: correlations alone do not establish horizontal transfer, selection, inheritance mechanisms or a saturation ceiling.')
p('For terreus, first split deep species comparisons from within-species structure, then examine independently defined MG labels. MG1 and MG2 each have three measured local isolates; MG3 has five. These groups support descriptive prevalence/heatmaps, but a small nominal P value from many non-independent pairs is not evidence of a well-powered association. Use biological-isolate resampling, uncertainty intervals and quality/annotation sensitivity; avoid defining groups from the same accessory matrix and then treating group differences as independent validation.')
add('<h3>Additional QC worth adding selectively</h3>')
p('Contamination screening can cover genome FASTAs even without raw reads; '+web('https://github.com/ncbi/fcs','NCBI FCS-GX')+' is a suitable candidate. Where matching reliable reads exist, '+web('https://github.com/marbl/merqury','Merqury')+' can add k-mer completeness and consensus QV, with read depth/error bias considered. Ploidy/depth/k-mer checks are useful for suspicious duplication or contamination. Reference-based structural assessment is useful only with an appropriate reference and careful interpretation of real biological divergence. These checks supplement rather than replace the identity, callability and provenance repairs above.')
end()

section('metadata','Circular-tree metadata: available now and fields still needed')
p('Use one canonical manifest keyed by assembly_id and linked to biological isolate_id. Preserve reported species separately from phylogenetically reviewed species. Tree-tip aliases, sequencing-run IDs and DTO/CBS/ATCC names should be linked identifiers, not interchangeable strings.')
table(['Metadata track','Available evidence','Rendering and missing-data policy'],[
 ['Taxon / reference role','Current labels: 55 terreus, 4 hortae, 3 pseudoterreus, 2 alabamensis, 1 aureoterreus, 1 floccosus. These are labels, not independently confirmed taxonomy.','Discrete taxon ring; type/ex-type symbol only with sourced evidence. Unknown taxonomy remains explicit.'],
 ['Study versus reference; assembly provenance','Local and public/reference assets exist, including alternative assemblies of named strains.','One source ring or tip marker; linked biological replicate flag; retain accession/version and source FASTA hash in the manifest.'],
 ['MG classification','samples.tsv and workbook support MG1: 39/50/73; MG2: 11/48/57; MG3: 26/40/47/56/67. Isolate 29 and R22/R23/R24 lack assigned MG in inspected metadata.','Discrete ring, grey unassigned. Do not infer MG from colour proximity or force groups into tree sectors.'],
 ['DTO / collection date / locality','Environmental Isolates sheet A1:E13: 12 isolates with DTO, dates from 22 July to 3 September 2019, location codes KU/KB/I/SZ/IL.','DTO in tip label or appendix; date/location better in aligned detail panel. Preserve date precision and source codes until expanded meanings are verified.'],
 ['Environment / host / clinical status','The 12 workbook rows are explicitly environmental. Metadata for R22/R23/R24 is incomplete; no basis here for assigning clinical source.','One source-category track with explicit unknown. NCBI submission date must not stand in for collection date.'],
 ['Read availability and analysis eligibility','Raw reads, fastp summaries and mapping results exist for different subsets. Current inventory has demonstrated false negatives.','Separate raw reads present from read analysis completed; genome-only references remain eligible for genome QC and appropriate sequence analyses.'],
 ['BUSCO / assembly confidence','Genome, transcript and embedded annotation scores are available with different lineages/modes.','One consistent genome completeness track plus a separate quality-detail panel. Retain C/S/D/F/M, lineage version, mode and input identity.'],
 ['Marker availability / copy status','Current availability quantified; copy identity still unresolved.','Three adjacent binary/status tracks or one summary ring; distinguish unique orthologue, partial, ambiguous duplicate and not recovered.'],
 ['Antifungal measurements','Antifungal resistance sheet B1:J16: CAS/AmB/VRC/POS paired columns for 12 isolates; observed -1/-2 values match within each drug/isolate.','Use raw measurements only after units, endpoint (including MIC versus MEC), method and meaning of paired columns are confirmed. Do not assume independent replicates.'],
 ['Functional biology','BGC/dbCAN data available; SignalP held; lov locus evidence needs synteny/copy adjudication.','Prefer a separate heatmap. Only a small number of validated categorical functions should occupy tree rings.'],
 ['Public accession and annotation provenance','Archived NCBI tables contain assembly accession/version, level, size/N50, BioProject/BioSample and annotation fields.','Keep full values in linked sample table. Source and assembly submission date are provenance, not sample collection metadata.']])
p('A polished main circular panel should contain about four to six compact tracks, not every available column: study/reference, taxon or MG, raw-read availability, a consistent QC metric and a marker-coverage track are good candidates. Place detailed collection information, four drug measurements and functional matrices beside the tree or in companion panels. Distinguish measured zero, inferred absence, no detection, not tested and not applicable in the legend.')
p('Minimum manifest fields: isolate_id, assembly_id, analysis_release_id, aliases, assembly_accession_version, assembly_sha256, read_ids, annotation_release/hash, reported_taxon, curated_taxon, type_status/evidence, study/reference status, MG and source, DTO, collection_date/precision, location/source, QC mode/lineage/version, marker coordinates/copy decision, per-analysis status/reason, phenotype value/unit/method/endpoint/replicate and original worksheet coordinates.')
p('Workbook evidence is preserved in <a href="spreadsheet_metadata_evidence.json">the extracted metadata audit</a>; it does not establish clinical resistance categories. Source: '+local('inbox/SNP_difference.xlsx')+'.')
end()

section('markers','Technical policy for missing or duplicated taxonomic loci')
p('BenA, CaM and RPB2 provide a bridge to established multigene Aspergillus taxonomy, but a marker name or best sequence hit alone does not establish the correct orthologue. Use curated, preferably type/ex-type-linked reference sequences and align homologous regions. '+web('https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7426331/','Houbraken and colleagues’ taxonomic framework')+'.')
table(['Case','Technical assessment','Main phylogeny policy'],[
 ['No transcript hit','BLASTn against transcripts and genomic FASTA; if needed, protein-to-genome tBLASTn and a splice-aware protein alignment such as miniprot/exonerate. Inspect contig boundaries and masked sequence.','Mark not recovered until adjudicated. Transcript absence alone is not genomic deletion; retain isolate with explicit missing characters if sufficient other evidence exists.'],
 ['Soft-masked or hard-masked locus','Lowercase soft masking retains sequence and can be searched with appropriate masking settings. Ns in hard-masked sequence cannot reconstruct lost bases; obtain original unmasked assembly if available.','Do not fill bases by guessing from another isolate. Preserve missing data and distinguish unavailable sequence from deletion.'],
 ['Several HSPs','Group by genomic interval, strand and expected exon structure; split hits may be one intron-containing gene or fragmented assembly rather than duplicated loci.','Count biological loci after grouping, not raw BLAST rows. Do not choose a top hit solely because it ranks first.'],
 ['Two or more plausible loci','Retain all hits; compare coverage, identity, coding integrity, neighbouring genes/synteny and locus gene trees. Examine known related tubulin paralogues when selecting BenA. Check haplotigs/contamination; use read depth where available.','Choose one only if orthology is justified. If unresolved, use missing data for that locus in the primary concatenation and show alternative-copy sensitivity analyses. Never concatenate arbitrary copies or manufacture a consensus.'],
 ['True duplication supported','Record both copy IDs/coordinates and duplication evidence; evaluate whether one orthologous copy remains comparable across samples.','A paralogue-aware gene tree is the appropriate primary evidence. A duplication is not automatically a reason to remove the whole isolate.'],
 ['Transcript-only asset','Can support expressed coding markers and protein/orthogroup work if identity and annotation provenance are valid; cannot demonstrate genome-wide copy number or recover absent introns.','Include in eligible gene-level panels; do not silently present it as a complete genome or a full Sanger amplicon.'],
 ['Genome plus Sanger references','Extract the homologous published amplicon windows, including introns where relevant; inspect boundaries and orientation. Full CDS/long genomic RPB2 and short Sanger fragments are not equivalent coverage.','Use explicit partitions and individual-locus trees; report the 26/32/8 current marker-coverage distribution and test sensitivity to missing-data patterns.']])
p('Retain a machine-readable all-hit audit: query/reference accession, genome hash, target contig/start/end/strand, identity, aligned coverage, exon/frame status, masking/edge flags, candidate locus count, selected orthologue and decision reason. Coverage/identity cutoffs should be validated per locus and taxonomic scope rather than imposed as one universal percentage. '+web('https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK279684/table/appendices.T.tblastn_application_options/','NCBI tBLASTn documentation')+'.')
end()

section('gates','Completion gates and a sensible order of work')
table(['Gate','Required work','Acceptance condition'],[[g[0]+' · '+g[1],g[2],g[3]] for g in gates])
p('Start with G0 because every later figure depends on reliable identity. G1 and input repair in G2 can then proceed by eligible analysis subset. G3 establishes the phylogenetic backbone; G4 supplies comparable functional/orthogroup matrices. G5 is the final figure release. Some descriptive diagnostics can be drafted now, as supplied here, without pretending that all inferential gates have passed.')
p('No raw reads is a valid reason to omit mapping, read-based SNP/SV/CNV or read-derived QV. It is not a reason to exclude a good genome FASTA from assembly QC, genome BUSCO, marker extraction or appropriately standardized gene-content comparisons. Transcript-only material has a narrower role. Every reference should be inventoried; inclusion in a specific plot follows eligibility and declared scope, not a requirement to fabricate unavailable measurements.')
end()

section('scope','Review scope, evidence and deliverables')
p('This is a targeted deep audit across the active analysis families, not a checksum validation of every raw file or a rerun of the entire project. It covers the prior chronological catalogue, selected run logs and configuration, 24 workflow step documents, five notebooks, all 4,661 selected alignment blocks across 66 samples, OG membership/counts, all current marker rows, QC summaries, 67 SignalP and EffectorP outputs, functional summaries, selected variant headers, the stored MST, workbook metadata and the named comparison projects. No full BAM/VCF event validation, assembly contamination run or wet-lab validation was performed.')
p('Evidence priority: actual output/log observations > saved code and recipes > inferred provenance. In particular, the first audit compared concatenation against a lexical locus order and found a mismatch; the subsequent exact-order audit resolves it completely. The final result is zero mismatches and continuous full coverage. The first diagnostic must not be misreported as a damaged concatenation.')
table(['Evidence file','Contents'],[
 ['<a href="audit_evidence.json">audit_evidence.json</a>','Actual tree log extracts, cohort IDs, OG counts/membership checks, marker availability, QC comparisons, output coverage, notebook errors and protein-ID checks.'],
 ['<a href="concatenation_order_verification.json">concatenation_order_verification.json</a>','Recovered locus order and coordinates; exact all-sample block comparison, zero mismatches.'],
 ['<a href="spreadsheet_metadata_evidence.json">spreadsheet_metadata_evidence.json</a>','Read-only extraction of antifungal and environmental metadata cells.'],
 ['<a href="global_status_and_gates.json">global_status_and_gates.json</a>','Structured stage status, ambiguities, completion gates and sensible uses.'],
 ['<a href="marker_availability_audit.svg">Marker availability SVG</a> · <a href="marker_availability_audit.pdf">PDF</a>','Audit figure from existing alignments; no copy-number or deletion inference.'],
 ['<a href="orthogroup_inventory_audit.svg">Orthogroup inventory SVG</a> · <a href="orthogroup_inventory_audit.pdf">PDF</a>','Audit figure from existing classic OG matrix.'],
 ['<a href="../2026-11-02/chronological_catalogue.json">Prior chronological catalogue</a>','Selected-file chronology and earlier identity comparisons; not an assumption that newer timestamps establish analytical validity.']])
p('Audit source scripts are in the C: workspace: audit_latest_outputs.py, verify_concatenation_order.py and build_deep_review.py. The original D: project and E: Listeria comparison were only read. No analysis was installed, restarted, repaired or overwritten during this review.')
end()
